  "text": "The place where someone lives.\n\nThe boat and the broken bridge\n\nNot the same as another thing.\n\nA craft that travels on water.\n\nAt the time something happens.\n\nM112 111q42-10 112 0l24 89H92Z\n\nWater that has fallen as rain.\n\nWelcome everyone in the garden\n\nYour answer, in your own words\n\n.g-practice-heading .g-primary\n\nIn the direction of something.\n\nThe liquid in rivers and rain.\n\nPip gives Grandma Mara's page.\n\nTalk about something together.\n\nMara’s message reached Grandma\n\nYour place is saved at picture\n\nMoving from inside to outside.\n\nListen to the person speaking.\n\nShort for that is or that has.\n\ng-choice-reading g-text-button\n\nThe whole amount or every one.\n\nWithout being hurt or damaged.\n\nThe inner surface of the hand.\n\nRelease ropes to move sections\n\nThe story view needs a moment.\n\nHere, a single musical sound.\n\nYour suggested ending for Sol\n\n“Is that a story?” Pip asked.\n\nThe prepared ending Sol chose\n\nWater that falls from clouds.\n\nKeep your promise to Grandma.\n\nPrepared and able to be used.\n\nWith nobody or nothing in it.\n\nBring something back to mind.\n\nGarden-side end not fastened.\n\nMainly; for the largest part.\n\nPREVIEW · YOUR GATHERING PLAN\n\nMoved or travelled somewhere.\n\nA point where two edges meet.\n\nThe lowest part of something.\n\nSuitable, useful or pleasing.\n\nNot shaking or changing much.\n\nLook at something for a time.\n\nNot fastened firmly in place.\n\nNo longer moved or continued.\n\non the dock side of the river\n\nBelonging to Rina, the baker.\n\nMake something reach farther.\n\nMoved back and forth loosely.\n\nM8 9q18-7 37 0v46q-19-6-37 0Z\n\nGrow higher or become larger.\n\nDid a task or made an effort.\n\nGuide which way a boat moves.\n\nHear Grandma’s offer for Mara\n\nSelect words from your ending\n\nThe ending of Pip’s adventure\n\nA possibility you can choose.",
